# IDE / Editor files
# .idea and the module files are never shared: they hold machine-local paths, and the
# module file names the platform jars one machine happens to have. Every clone imports
# WigellAutoCore/autocore/pom.xml as a Maven project instead, and IntelliJ picks the
# right JavaFX classifier for that operating system.
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/
.agents/
.project
.classpath
run.sh
.mise.toml
.mise.*.toml

# Build output
out/
bin/
target/
*.class
# The file list start.sh generates for javac; created and deleted on every run
sources.txt

# Local database, created by the app and not to be version controlled.
# The leading slash anchors the rule to the repository root; otherwise it would
# also match the source folder com/wac/autocore/data/ and new files there would vanish.
# Without a trailing slash the rule also matches a link, not just a folder: the database
# lives on the NVMe and data is a link to it.
/data
*.db
# The one exception: a database from before the migrations, kept read-only as the fixture for
# the L3 proof. Nothing opens it for writing; every run copies it to /tmp first.
!WigellAutoCore/autocore/test/data/autocore-original.db

# Secrets: never in the repository. Configuration holds placeholders, the values come from the
# environment. See "Hemligheter" in README.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.jks
*.keystore
secrets.properties

# Archives & Temporary files
*.zip
*.pdf
RetrospektDagbok.md

# The proof runs belong to the delivery, not to the code. They are recorded on the machine
# that ran them and kept beside the repository, so a pull never writes over someone else's.
/bevis/

# Personal test reports and local results
rapport.md
rapport*.md
ARKITEKTUR_OCH_DESIGNMONSTER.md

# OS files
*.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# JVM crash logs
hs_err_pid*.log

